wild savage and unstoppable the Norse  berserkers were almost more beasts than  man these Warriors were once just men  but through their ritualistic practices  they acquired powers that made them more  than just a formidable foe there have  been many tales of these wild men who  charged into battle wearing nothing but  the fur of animals who feel no pain or  fear the berserker warriors are known  for being able to enter a rage field  trance their bodies would convulse their  teeth would grind and chatter until the  rage had taken over their bodies would  even change color with their faces  turning a dark red or purple to match  the intense rage while stillness trance  the berserkers are believed to have  superhuman strength and speed they were  almost unstoppable as they were able to  ignore pain being able to fight through  cuts slashes and even the loss of limbs  ignoring wounds that would render a  normal man useless they have been  described as almost possessed while in  this state and sometimes they cannot  discern the difference between enemy and  Ally there are varying explanations for  the behavior of the Berserker warriors  some believe their practices to be  similar to that of shamans or druids  sharing a bond with nature and its  surroundings they believe that an animal  spirit can live on after death and  through wearing the fur pelts of animals  the berserk Warriors are emboldened gain  in what they believe to be the animal  strength and abilities the pelt of a  bear was thought to give him in strength  and courage the wolf's ferocity and  prowess and the stag guile and speed  although these Berserker Warriors are  part of a tribe or pack they clearly  preferred the company of animals they  would only ever harm animals in times of  famine and the animal sacrifice was  someone of a ritual they would often  drink the blood of the animal  symbolizing the parson of life and  strength  these type of as Urkel warriors would  often wield large hammers and axes or  even duel hatchets weapons that could be  swung around wildly with little or no  concern of their surroundings this could  also be seen in their wild and  unpredictable fighting style there is a  possibility that the werewolf legend  could have originated from the Berserker  warriors essentially transforming from  man to beast in battle  these Berserker Warriors were often used  as frontline shock troops they would  often be sent to disrupt and shock the  enemy sometimes even causing them to  flee just with their sheer ferocity some  historians believe that the behavior of  the Berserker warriors does have a  scientific explanation opposed to being  possessed by animal spirits the  Berserker warriors frenzy of rage and  uncontrollable anger may have been  caused from the consumption of the plant  bog Myrtle a spice used in alcoholic  beverages combined with other  hallucinogenics that they may have  inhaled in the wild  berserkers may have been under the  influence of alcohol or drug like  substances this would explain their  disregard for pain and unpredictable  behavior there is a tale from Icelandic  poet who mentions a berserker warrior  who ate his own shield in the middle of  battle when he was done he then killed  six other men there is no definitive  proof to whether the Berserker Warriors  charged into battle possessed by the  spirits of animals or in a self-induced  trance caused by alcohol and other  hallucinogenics it is down to your own  interpretation the risen of a type of  Berserker which much closer resembles a  Viking warrior these Warriors worship  the Norse god Odin these berserkers were  considered to be born warriors with a  thirst for battle in battle these  Warriors were still similar entering  rage-filled trances but it's believed  that these trances were driven by their  need to be victorious there was no  greater honor to them and taken a man's  life in battle  whether you believe that the Berserker  Warriors had magical gifts bestowed upon  them by animal spirits or that there  were just a bunch of drunk crazy Vikings  they were undoubtedly fierce warriors  who were feared by enemies everywhere  and even allies if you were unlucky  enough to come face-to-face with a  berserker it is likely that their face  would be the last you'd ever see if  you've enjoyed this video then please  consider leaving a thumbs up as it helps  promote the video and allows the channel  to grow if there's anything you'd like  to discuss or have any ideas for future  videos then please let me know in the  comment section as always I've been your  host mythology in fiction explained
 

